202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Analyzing the impact of all these features over time, it is possible to see a story of polarization: The Periphery has become a worse place for commuters: this is probably due to the fact that the infrastructure in these outer rings has likely failed to keep up with population growth, creating severe bottlenecks. Small Towns have become a lot less relevant to the commuting problem, meanwhile, the legendary efficiency of Medium Towns is fading.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
